<BaseLayout title="About" description="About The Margin of Error and Hans W. A. Hanley.">
	<section class="standard-page about-page">
		<header class="page-heading">
			<p class="kicker">Colophon</p>
			<h1>About the margin</h1>
		</header>
		<div class="about-grid">
			<div class="prose">
				<p class="standfirst">
					I’m <a href="https://www.hanshanley.com/">Hans W. A. Hanley</a>. I write The
					Margin of Error to make sense of politics and public life with the tools I know
					best: code, data, and close reading.
				</p>
				<p>
					I’m especially interested in how information moves through networks, how
					political narratives take hold, and what the available evidence can—and
					cannot—tell us. That has led me to write about disinformation, news media,
					elections, democracy, and international affairs.
				</p>
				<p>
					This site brings together essays first published on Google Sites and Substack,
					work published elsewhere, and new writing. When an article grows out of an
					analysis, I include the code, data, or interactive work so readers can follow how
					I reached the conclusion.
				</p>
			</div>
			<aside class="about-aside">
				<p class="kicker">Elsewhere</p>
				<a href="https://www.hanshanley.com/">Academic work</a>
				<a href="https://github.com/hanshanley">GitHub</a>
				<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeHPhVHdJ0xdCYq3wDYjkOIxgVdErP4qszNOBQYrnyzTz3xyQ/viewform">Subscribe</a>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
